{"type":"npc","name":"Paradoxical Past","folder":"lBiU967QOX7QFRzY","system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":150,"temp":0,"max":150,"details":""},"ac":{"value":27,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":30}],"details":""},"resistances":[{"type":"mental","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["astral","chronan"],"details":"Telepathy 120 feet, Truespeech"},"level":{"value":9},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>When a paradox is created in time travel, entire lives can be erased. The souls lost to such time loops can end up adrift in the Astral Plane, endlessly reliving moments from their past. Unable to accept their fate, a paradoxical past often winds up doing the same things over and over again, expecting a different result.</p><hr /><p>Temporal paradoxes are a rare category of spirits that arise when strong-willed individuals are separated from their rightful place in the timeline. Though they retain strong memories and emotional connections to their pasts, it is seldom possible for them to go back to where they came from. Even if they were to manage the daunting task of locating their original reality and timeline, it would fundamentally reject their return. This rejection stems from a combination of their former realities editing them out in the interest of self-stabilization and the influence of their new realities causing their old homes to recognize them as incompatible invaders. Unfortunately for temporal paradoxes, their new realities don't fully accept them either, making them vulnerable to unwelcome twists of fate.</p><h2>Fractured Memories</h2><p>A paradoxical past can learn—but as they recycle bits of their past from moment to moment, they can't be relied upon to retain that learning. At one moment, a paradoxical past might be friendly and disposed to help the party, while a minute later they've never seen the party before and are inclined to attack them as trespassers. Later, the paradoxical past might once again recognize the party and wonder why everyone has their weapons drawn.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 90/200/360 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Deception, Intimidation, Occultism)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, constitution, dexterity, energy resistant (vitality), mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.SwUiVavHKMWG7t5K]{Truespeech}), spirit, strength, throwing, time, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Ryan King","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":6},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":18,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"thoughtsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":30}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":21,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":16,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":19},"athletics":{"base":17},"deception":{"base":19},"intimidation":{"base":17},"occultism":{"base":16}},"traits":{"value":["astral"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"4smcNzAu4KRcmSr3","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/paradoxical-past.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Paradoxical Past","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/paradoxical-past.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff